  "description": "HANTEY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H24 F72 O37 Yb8 2-,2(C42 H31 N4 O2 1+),0.5(C6 H14),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb7 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb8 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.328-4.307 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.29-145.04°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [HL]2[Yb8(hfac)12(OH)12(O)]·0.5C6H14·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
